      "text": "Metrics Built to Serve Model Foundry\n\nThe key metrics I focused on were:\n\n1. Model Activity Metrics\n\nThese helped determine whether a model was active, stale, or unused.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Last online inference time\n* Last offline inference time\n* 7-day active model detection\n* Inference call counts\n* Online vs offline usage\n* Registered vs actively serving models\n\nThese metrics helped teams quickly identify whether a model was still being used in production.\n\n2. Performance Metrics\n\nThese helped teams understand runtime behavior.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Model inference latency\n* Online serving latency\n* Query response latency for model pages\n* Model page loading performance\n\nOne improvement was reducing online active model page load time from roughly 12–15 seconds to under 4 seconds, \nand improving registered model page latency to around 1 second.\n\n3. Feature Health Metrics\n\nThese helped model owners understand whether their input features were reliable.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Feature availability\n* Live vs dead feature status\n* Training-only features\n* Holdout features\n* Excluded feature reasons\n* Feature-to-model-group mapping\n\nThis helped teams debug model quality issues and understand feature dependency risk.\n\n4. Dataset Freshness Metrics\n\nThese helped offline model owners understand whether their upstream datasets were fresh.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Offline dataset freshness\n* HDFS freshness\n* Openhouse freshness\n* Daily freshness snapshots\n* Dataset-level health status\n\nThis gave teams better visibility into stale or delayed offline training and inference dependencies.\n\n5. Compliance and Metadata Metrics\n\nThese helped teams track governance readiness.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Model card availability\n* Model ownership\n* Compliance metadata completeness\n* Model version metadata\n* Deployment metadata\n* AI Act-related model documentation status\n\nThis became important as compliance moved from project-level tracking to model-level tracking.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Metrics Built to Serve Model Foundry\n\nThe key metrics I focused on were:\n\n1. Model Activity Metrics\n\nThese helped determine whether a model was active, stale, or unused.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Last online inference time\n* Last offline inference time\n* 7-day active model detection\n* Inference call counts\n* Online vs offline usage\n* Registered vs actively serving models\n\nThese metrics helped teams quickly identify whether a model was still being used in production.\n\n2. Performance Metrics\n\nThese helped teams understand runtime behavior.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Model inference latency\n* Online serving latency\n* Query response latency for model pages\n* Model page loading performance\n\nOne improvement was reducing online active model page load time from roughly 12–15 seconds to under 4 seconds, \nand improving registered model page latency to around 1 second.\n\n3. Feature Health Metrics\n\nThese helped model owners understand whether their input features were reliable.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Feature availability\n* Live vs dead feature status\n* Training-only features\n* Holdout features\n* Excluded feature reasons\n* Feature-to-model-group mapping\n\nThis helped teams debug model quality issues and understand feature dependency risk.\n\n4. Dataset Freshness Metrics\n\nThese helped offline model owners understand whether their upstream datasets were fresh.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Offline dataset freshness\n* HDFS freshness\n* Openhouse freshness\n* Daily freshness snapshots\n* Dataset-level health status\n\nThis gave teams better visibility into stale or delayed offline training and inference dependencies.\n\n5. Compliance and Metadata Metrics\n\nThese helped teams track governance readiness.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Model card availability\n* Model ownership\n* Compliance metadata completeness\n* Model version metadata\n* Deployment metadata\n* AI Act-related model documentation status\n\nThis became important as compliance moved from project-level tracking to model-level tracking.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
